# Repository-root ignores.
#
# Added by Production MS4. `backend/.gitignore` and `frontend/.gitignore` already covered their own
# trees, but nothing covered the root — so a `.env` written next to `docker-compose.yml` (which is
# exactly where its header tells you to put one) was tracked by default. Nothing of the sort has
# ever been committed; this makes that a property of the repository rather than of everyone's care.

### Env — real values, never committed. `.env.example` / `.env.production.example` are the ###
### placeholder-only templates and are deliberately NOT ignored.                           ###
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

### Local-disk fake storage (pronto.storage.mode=local) at the repository root ###
/data/

### QA scratch files (manual smoke-test payloads/output, not fixtures) ###
qa-tmp/
qa-tmp-*/

### OS / editor ###
.DS_Store
